          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em numerable open cover
            (alias
            = succeed ")" do
              %em normal cover
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            that admits a subordinate
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i\}
            be an open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (actually
            %a{:href => "#Dold63"} Dold 1963
            doesn’t always require open, see discussion below). It is said to be
            %strong numerable
            if there is a collection of
